    "body": "## Chat05A server-authorized voting and authored-text triggers\n\n### Implemented\n- Server-owned person registry and immutable battle-to-person bindings for both participants.\n- Individually issued spectator bearer capabilities; D1 stores only secret hashes, supports generation-based revocation/reissue, and derives ballot identity from the bearer. Participants and unbound spectators cannot vote.\n- Stable `deriveSocialVoteId(battleId)`; unique database constraints enforce one vote per battle and one immutable ballot per person. Replays, reloads, Worker restarts, and concurrent requests retain the same vote/ballot.\n- Trusted, versioned ready-phrase offers are pinned by the operator before commits. Synthetic fixtures are test-only; no game-canon phrases were invented.\n- Attack and defense final text are authenticated, server-compared with frozen Unicode 15.0 full case-fold normalization, and committed atomically with the participant lifecycle transition. Browser provenance, source phrase, side, or edit flags are not trusted. Other-side final text stays hidden until reveal.\n- Reveal computes exactly one trigger: `DRAW`, `AUTHORED_TEXT`, `BOTH`, or `NONE`. Vote row and authoritative reveal are in one D1 batch; `mechanicalOutcome` is unchanged. Required social/recognized outcomes remain `PENDING`; the legacy finalize path rejects pending triggers.\n- Migration `0010` expands trigger reasons while preserving existing vote and ballot rows and foreign-key integrity. Lifecycle Web/docs mirrors are byte-identical.\n\n### Exact-head evidence\nHEAD: `99d4322dc1a9fba76f113f32db93829bf4c64407`  \nParent: `7ac0dd95a333dceead07a0c78dc8377f0c2e7cde`  \nBase: `main@b435e70eb88b87b3c3324ef2a2da14cdf473f229`\n\n- GitHub Actions on this HEAD: [Private Gameplay API / isolated local Workerd-D1 #41089043386](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/41089043386), [CAS SQL / Wrangler local D1 #41089043899](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/41089043899), and [AI forensics capture #41089043465](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/41089043465) all succeeded.\n- CI log explicitly reports migrations 0001–0010 and the DRAW / BOTH / A_WIN / B_WIN / NONE trigger matrix. Local pure contract tests: 9/9. Local SQLite migration/CAS suite: 11/11.\n- Independent `critical_reviewer`: `PASS_CRITICAL_REVIEW` on this exact HEAD, including authorization, atomic reveal, migration preservation, legacy restore, and finalization bypass checks.\n\n### Acceptance boundary\nThis remains a Draft PR. These checks are source-level and isolated local Worker/D1 evidence. No hosted gameplay D1, deployed Worker, Safari/two-device acceptance, merge, or deploy is claimed. No Chat05B, Chat05C, NPC, timers, economy, UI, or Cloudflare operation is included.",
